\section{Embedded Microcomputer Systems}

\begin{description}

\item [Embedded:] Special purpose computing devices.
Computers that are {\it embedded} or hidden inside something
else.  Examples:  SmartPhone, Copier machine controller, Automotive Anti-lock
braking system, Automotive Engine Control system, Battery Management System, 
Airliner autopilot,  DVD player, Roku Box, IOT devices: Smart
Thermostat, Smart light bulb, Security camera.

\item [Microcomputer:] A computer you can buy for \$1 - \$100.
Almost all of the same software and hardware issues we will study
have been around since the 1960's.  The only thing different is
the cost of the hardware.  All of the following had {\it  essentially}
the exact same {\it software environment} to what we are studying in this class:

<s>\end{description}
<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
<s>\begin{description}\item

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|l|}
\hline
Era             &       Technology        & Cost \\ \hline
1960's          &       Mainframe         & \$1M \\ \hline
1970's          &       Minicomputer      & \$100k \\ \hline
1980's          &       PC's              & \$5k   \\ \hline
1990's          &       Cellphone         & \$500  \\ \hline
2000's          &       Microcontroller   & \$50  \\ \hline
2010's          &       Microcontroller   & \$5   \\ \hline
2020's          &       \href{https://www.wch.cn/products/CH32V003.html}{WCH CH32V003}   & \$0.10  \\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}


<s>\end{description}
<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
<s>\begin{description}

\item[Systems:]   From ``The Random House Dictionary'' \\
{\small\tt  \begin{quote} {\bf 1. } a group or combination of things or parts forming a complex or unified
  whole.\\
  ... \\
  {\bf 5. } a set of body organs or related tissues concerned with the same function.\\
  ...\\
  {\bf 7. } Often: an organized set of computer programs.
  \end{quote}
}

\end{description}

<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}


\subsection{ECE 474 Key Ideas:}
\begin{itemize}
        \item C programming for Java programmers.
        \item advanced C programming (void pointers etc.)
        \item Process Context, Multi-tasking, Basic schedulers
        \item Interrupt service routines
        \item Meeting real-time performance constraints, scheduling algorithms.
        \item Mutual exclusion via semaphores
             and coordination of resources shared between multiple tasks.
%         \item Fundamentals of TCP/IP Network Communication. 
        \item Bit-level I/O to hardware devices.
        \item Use of the FreeRTOS real-time kernel.
        \item Integration, test, and performance characterization of
        embedded real time systems in the lab.
\end{itemize}


<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}

\subsection{Pre-requisites}
\begin{itemize}
        \item  You must have completed two quarters programming in java or C.
        \item  Basic understanding of computer organization and architecture.
        \item  Understanding and use of electronic laboratory instrumentation.
\end{itemize}


