\subsection{Fundamental Problem: Combinatorial Complexity}

<*n> For both your lab team {\it and} the project itself, you have the problem of managing the interactions between agents.  Let's take a look at how many interactions you have as the number of agents increases:

<*>
2 Agents
\includegraphics[width=2.0in]{intro_figs/00282.eps}
2 interactions


3 Agents
 \includegraphics[width=2.0in]{intro_figs/00283.eps}
6 interactions


4 Agents
 \includegraphics[width=2.0in]{intro_figs/00284.eps}
12 interactions


<*>
<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
\subsubsection{In-class Exercise}

What is the general expression for number of interactions between $n$ agents?

<n> Answer: $n(n-1)$

<*>
